WEBVTT

NOTE map-navigation: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.453
Read the pins, move the moisture bands,

V0-2
00:00:05.553 --> 00:00:09.020
switch to variance, and
filter what the map shows.

V1a-1
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.725
Each sprinkler of a station scanned in
the past seven days is a pin at its own

V1a-2
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:23.418
coordinates. A pin scanned today is filled
with the colour of the moisture band

V1a-3
00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:28.170
its reading falls into, and a pin last
scanned on an earlier day is drawn clear.

V1b-1
00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:35.593
Four bands by default: 0 to 5, 6 to
19, 20 to 30, and above 30 percent.

V2a-1
00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:45.472
The colour bar under the
legend has draggable handles.

V2a-2
00:00:45.572 --> 00:00:48.406
Move one and the map
recolours when you let go.

V2b-1
00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:52.746
Dragging a handle changes the boundary
and saves it to your preferences.

V3a-1
00:00:59.753 --> 00:01:03.603
The button beside the legend
toggles between VWC and variance.

V3b-1
00:01:04.086 --> 00:01:08.164
Variance colours each pin by how
far it sits from its own target

V3b-2
00:01:08.264 --> 00:01:12.216
instead of by its raw reading:
three bands, centred on target.

V4a-1
00:01:19.173 --> 00:01:24.223
Layers chooses which stations are drawn:
all of them, or only the enabled ones.

V4b-1
00:01:24.706 --> 00:01:29.726
Disabled stations are not being adjusted,
so hiding them leaves only the heads

V4b-2
00:01:29.826 --> 00:01:34.526
your push will affect. Layers saves
your choice to your user preferences.

V5a-1
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.155
Selecting a station in the
table highlights it on the map,

V5a-2
00:01:45.255 --> 00:01:47.370
and selecting a pin selects the row.

V5b-1
00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:49.959
One selection, shown in both panels.

V5b-2
00:01:50.059 --> 00:01:52.873
Use whichever is faster
to find the head you mean.
